  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Peraton obligated $1.9B in federal contract dollars in FY2026 to date. Peraton won 296 awards so far, with an average award size of $6.5M, and obligations are down 7.3% year over year. Peraton received the largest share of obligations from the General Services Administration, which obligated $639M, followed by the Department of Defense with $380M and the Department of Transportation with $315M. Computer Systems Design Services is Peraton's largest market, with $982M in obligations, followed by Engineering Services with $394M and Custom Computer Programming Services with $183M. Historical obligations show growth from $466M in FY21 to $2.1B in FY25, with FY26 at $1.9B so far. This profile shows where Peraton is concentrated by agency and by NAICS market through the current fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How large are Peraton's FY2026 federal obligations?",
        "body": "Peraton obligated $1.9B in FY2026 to date. Peraton's award count is 296 and the average award size is $6.5M. Peraton's obligations are down 7.3% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Peraton's top buyers and what markets drive those obligations?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration is Peraton's top buyer with $639M in obligations, followed by the Department of Defense with $380M and the Department of Transportation with $315M. Computer Systems Design Services is Peraton's largest market with $982M, followed by Engineering Services with $394M and Custom Computer Programming Services with $183M. Other notable markets include Other Computer Related Services at $126M and All Other Telecommunications at $116M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Peraton make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Peraton made $1.9B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Peraton won 296 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $6.5M, and obligations are down 7.3% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Peraton?",
      "a": "Peraton's largest buyers are the General Services Administration with $639M, the Department of Defense with $380M, and the Department of Transportation with $315M. Other buying agencies include the National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $182M and the Department of Health and Human Services with $143M."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Peraton sell to the government?",
      "a": "Peraton sells primarily Computer Systems Design Services, which account for $982M in obligations, and Engineering Services, which account for $394M. Peraton also sells Custom Computer Programming Services at $183M, Other Computer Related Services at $126M, and telecommunications and related IT services in multiple NAICS categories."
